title Frontend classes - Start a sprint and change its active scope
top to bottom direction
skinparam class {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
class SprintsPage {
  +openStart(sprintId: Guid): void
  +openScope(sprintId: Guid): void
  +openCloseSprint(sprintId: Guid): void
}
note top of SprintsPage
SprintListView emits startRequested(sprintId)
and scopeRequested(sprintId) (plan-sprints);
workspaceName = layout.workspace().name.
Scope and close dialogs: offerSprintsLink = false.
Started: open the board, "Sprint 9 started"
toast. ModeChanged: layout.modeChanged().
Outdated: own counter + 1 (list rereads).
CloseSprint(sprint): openCloseSprint.
Scope Changed: counter + 1, "Scope updated"
toast with the summary; Outdated: counter + 1.
While a dialog is open: unconfirmed -> counter + 1
at once; forbidden -> "Your access changed" toast
via TOAST_SERVICE, without Retry.
end note
class SprintPlanningPage {
  +openStart(): void
  +openCloseSprint(sprintId: Guid): void
}
note top of SprintPlanningPage
SprintPlanView startRequested(sprintId) ->
openStart(), with the workspace name it read.
Started: open the board with the toast.
ModeChanged, Outdated: own counter + 1
(the plan header is reread).
CloseSprint(sprint): openCloseSprint.
While the dialog is open: unconfirmed -> counter + 1
at once; forbidden -> "Your access changed" toast
via TOAST_SERVICE, without Retry.
end note
class SprintBoardPage {
  -header: WritableSignal<ActiveSprintHeader?>
  +openStart(sprintId: Guid): void
  +openScope(): void
  +openRemove(card: BoardCard): void
  +openCloseSprint(sprintId: Guid): void
}
note top of SprintBoardPage
Change scope and Add stories: openScope() with
header().sprintId. BoardView removeRequested(card):
openRemove builds the ScopeStorySummary. Both pass
offerSprintsLink = true. No active
sprint: openStart(header().nextPlannedSprint.sprintId)
with workspaceName = layout.workspace().name.
Started: own counter + 1 with the toast. ModeChanged:
layout.modeChanged(). Outdated: counter + 1.
CloseSprint(sprint): openCloseSprint(sprint.sprintId).
Scope Changed: counter + 1 with the "Scope updated"
toast; Outdated: counter + 1.
While a dialog is open: unconfirmed -> counter + 1
at once; forbidden -> "Your access changed" toast
via TOAST_SERVICE, without Retry.
end note
class BacklogPage
note top of BacklogPage
Owned by work prioritize-work. Opens the dialog
with addStoryId and offerSprintsLink = true. A planned
sprint navigates to its plan with ?add={storyId} instead.
Changed reloads the backlog with the "Scope
updated" toast; Outdated and unconfirmed reload
it; forbidden: "Your access changed" toast,
without Retry.
end note
class "WorkItemDetailPage\nWorkHierarchyPage" as WorkPages {
  +openRemoveFromSprint(sprintId: Guid): void
}
note top of WorkPages
Owned by work delete-leaf-work. When WorkItemDeleteDialog
closes with RemoveFromSprint(sprintId), opens the dialog
in remove mode with the summary of its story and
offerSprintsLink = true.
Changed reloads the view with the "Scope updated"
toast; Outdated and unconfirmed reload it;
forbidden: "Your access changed" toast,
without Retry.
end note
class StartSprintDialog {
  +sprintId: InputSignal<Guid>
  +workspaceName: InputSignal<string>
  +unconfirmed: OutputEmitterRef<void>
  +forbidden: OutputEmitterRef<void>
  +close(outcome: StartSprintOutcome?): void
}
note right of StartSprintDialog
close(Started(result)) on started.
close(ModeChanged) when it closes after modeChanged.
close(Outdated) when it closes after outdated, or
at once on notFound.
close(CloseSprint(sprint)) at once on
closeSprintRequested.
close() on Cancel means dismissed.
Relays the view's unconfirmed and forbidden as
its own outputs and stays open.
end note
class StartSprintOutcome {
  +kind: Started | ModeChanged | Outdated | CloseSprint
  +started: SprintSaveResult?
  +sprint: SprintReference?
}
class SprintScopeDialog {
  +sprintId: InputSignal<Guid>
  +addStoryId: InputSignal<Guid?>
  +removeStoryId: InputSignal<Guid?>
  +removeStorySummary: InputSignal<ScopeStorySummary?>
  +offerSprintsLink: InputSignal<boolean>
  +draft: Signal<DraftState>
  +unconfirmed: OutputEmitterRef<void>
  +forbidden: OutputEmitterRef<void>
  +requestClose(): Promise<void>
  +close(outcome: SprintScopeOutcome?): void
}
note right of SprintScopeDialog
Inputs, offerSprintsLink included, pass straight
to SprintScopeForm.
close(Changed(summary)) on changed; close(Outdated)
when it closes after outdated, or at once on
notFound; close() on Cancel means dismissed.
Relays the form's unconfirmed and forbidden as
its own outputs and stays open with the selection.
requestClose on a dirty draft opens
UnsavedChangesDialog (CancelForm);
each opening page delegates its FormDraft to it.
end note
class SprintScopeOutcome {
  +kind: Changed | Outdated
  +changed: ScopeChangeSummary?
}
class ScopeChangeSummary {
  +saved: SprintSaveResult
  +summary: string
}
note bottom of ScopeChangeSummary
summary names the change for the opener's
"Scope updated" toast, e.g. "Volunteer check-in
list" was added to Sprint 8.
end note
class ScopeStorySummary {
  +storyId: Guid
  +key: string
  +title: string
  +status: WorkStatus
  +assigneeName: string?
  +completedTasks: int
  +totalTasks: int
  +estimate: int?
}
class SprintStartView {
  +sprintId: InputSignal<Guid>
  +workspaceName: InputSignal<string>
  -sprint: ResourceRef<SprintPlanResult>
  +started: OutputEmitterRef<SprintSaveResult>
  +modeChanged: OutputEmitterRef<void>
  +outdated: OutputEmitterRef<void>
  +notFound: OutputEmitterRef<void>
  +unconfirmed: OutputEmitterRef<void>
  +forbidden: OutputEmitterRef<void>
  +closeSprintRequested: OutputEmitterRef<SprintReference>
  +start(): Promise<void>
}
note right of SprintStartView
sprint = sprintPlanResource(...): summary and version;
no active-sprint check on open. Start sprint stays
disabled until it resolves; a failed read offers
Try again = sprint.reload() and Cancel.
A stale 409 calls sprint.reload() once.
409 active sprint: blocked-active; Review and close
emits closeSprintRequested(the sprint the 409 names).
409 Kanban: modeChanged. 409 not planned: outdated.
404: notFound. Unexpected 403: forbidden.
No response: "We couldn't confirm
whether Sprint 9 started"; emits unconfirmed;
sprint.reload() once. Still Planned: Start sprint
again; Active: neutral "Sprint 9 is active now."
with Close only, and outdated is emitted.
end note
class SprintScopeForm {
  +sprintId: InputSignal<Guid>
  +addStoryId: InputSignal<Guid?>
  +removeStoryId: InputSignal<Guid?>
  +removeStorySummary: InputSignal<ScopeStorySummary?>
  +offerSprintsLink: InputSignal<boolean>
  -sprint: ResourceRef<SprintPlanResult>
  -search: WritableSignal<string>
  -page: WritableSignal<int>
  -candidates: ResourceRef<SprintCandidatePage>
  -toAdd: WritableSignal<Set<Guid>>
  +changed: OutputEmitterRef<ScopeChangeSummary>
  +outdated: OutputEmitterRef<void>
  +notFound: OutputEmitterRef<void>
  +unconfirmed: OutputEmitterRef<void>
  +forbidden: OutputEmitterRef<void>
  +draftChange: OutputEmitterRef<DraftState>
  +submit(): Promise<void>
}
note right of SprintScopeForm
sprint = sprintPlanResource: title, dates and the version
the command carries; Add and Return to backlog stay disabled
until it resolves. candidates = sprintCandidatesResource with
eligibleOnly = true; toAdd is keyed by story ID and survives
search and paging. addStoryId joins toAdd only if one eligible
read with storyId = addStoryId returns it.
A stale 409, or no response (which also emits unconfirmed),
reloads the sprint and the candidates once and adopts the new
version; toAdd then drops each story now in this sprint, named
neutrally ("HCK-130 is already in Sprint 8"), and remove mode
names a story that left it. After no response, a sprint read
Closed shows the neutral "Sprint 8 is closed now." and emits
outdated. A 409 for a closed or still planned sprint emits
outdated; a 404 emits notFound; an unexpected 403 keeps the
selection and emits forbidden. A 400 or 409 naming stories to
add (Done, foreign, already a member, or in another open
sprint) marks each; a marked checkbox stays focusable
(aria-disabled) and takes focus first. A 400 naming the story
to remove as no longer a member drops it, named neutrally.
View sprints renders only while offerSprintsLink is true;
without it, Close is the first action and takes focus.
draftChange is dirty once toAdd differs from its opening set.
end note
interface ISprintService {
  +sprintPlanResource(query: () => GetSprintPlanQuery | undefined): ResourceRef<SprintPlanResult>
  +sprintCandidatesResource(query: () => GetSprintCandidatesQuery | undefined): ResourceRef<SprintCandidatePage>
  +start(command: StartSprintCommand): Promise<SprintSaveResult>
  +changeScope(command: ChangeSprintScopeCommand): Promise<SprintSaveResult>
}
note right of ISprintService
Reads are caller-owned signal resources defined by
plan-sprints; mutations return promises.
No RxJS type crosses api.
end note
class SprintService {
  -http: HttpClient
}
class CloseSprintDialog
note bottom of CloseSprintDialog
Defined by close-sprint; opened for the sprint
a CloseSprint outcome names.
end note
SprintsPage ..> StartSprintDialog : opens from startRequested(sprintId)
SprintPlanningPage ..> StartSprintDialog : opens (Start sprint)
SprintBoardPage ..> StartSprintDialog : opens (No active sprint: Start next)
SprintsPage ..> SprintScopeDialog : opens from scopeRequested(sprintId)
SprintBoardPage ..> SprintScopeDialog : opens (Change scope, Add stories, Remove)
BacklogPage ..> SprintScopeDialog : Add to sprint (active): add mode with addStoryId
WorkPages ..> SprintScopeDialog : opens in remove mode on WorkItemDeleteOutcome RemoveFromSprint(sprintId)
SprintBoardPage ..> ScopeStorySummary : builds from BoardCard
SprintsPage ..> CloseSprintDialog : on CloseSprint
SprintPlanningPage ..> CloseSprintDialog : on CloseSprint
SprintBoardPage ..> CloseSprintDialog : on CloseSprint
StartSprintDialog --> SprintStartView : composes
StartSprintDialog ..> StartSprintOutcome : close result
SprintScopeDialog --> SprintScopeForm : composes
SprintScopeDialog ..> SprintScopeOutcome : close result
SprintScopeOutcome --> ScopeChangeSummary
SprintStartView ..> ISprintService : inject token
SprintScopeForm ..> ISprintService : inject token
ISprintService <|.. SprintService
@enduml
